{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1412952-initiative-speciality","id":1412952,"title":"Initiative speciality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-10T20:22:14-07:00","id":1412952,"title":"Initiative speciality","content":"So tonight I was running my Werewolf the Wild West game. During combat, when it was time for initiative to be rolled, the Ragabash of the Pack tells me that he rolled a 25 out a Dex+Wits+s10 initiative roll. When I asked how he got that he yells me that he has a Wits Speciality of Initiative. Now with all the years that I have ST Werewolf, I have never come across that. I will admit that I love in a small town and that over the years, my rpg experience has been limited to bout 30 people. <br /> <br /> The purpose of this post is to ask ..officially, in canon, can a Specialty in Wits for Initiative have a 10 Again dice trick? Idk how I feel bout &quot;homebrewing&quot; that....<br /> <br /> Edit: to clarify i am using W20 for rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 09-10-2020, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T01:56:08-07:00","id":1412974,"title":"","content":"Way back in WtA 1e, Initiative was a Wits + Alertness roll with successes dictating order instead of 1d10 + Dex + Wits like it is now. Obviously the specialty made sense then. Unfortunately while the initiative roll has changed, references to Wits having a specialty in it tended to get copie